    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-black text-gray-900 tracking-tight mb-3">
      Closed-Cell Backer Rod Sizing: The 2:1 Joint Rule
    </h1>
    <p class="text-base text-gray-600 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mb-6">
      When sealing expansion joints in concrete driveways, sidewalks, or building facades, many DIYers assume that filling the entire depth of the joint with caulk creates the strongest seal. In polymer engineering, the exact opposite is true: thick, deep joints tear themselves apart! To allow modern polyurethane sealants to stretch up to 500% without splitting, you must install <strong>closed-cell foam backer rod governed by the engineered 2:1 width-to-depth ratio</strong>.
    </p>

